{"author":{"id":"0fb62b7075a4219f84b4bf8c9c235af1632f3fa4b63ca899f025ad8215a930fd"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1778070874,"nonce":"D8+lP34QWQXxFQUcsOIcaH9jIzU=","title":"data/masters.RDS is the only published artifact. RDS is R-only and opaque to anyone outside the R ecosystem, which is a poor fit for a dataset that is meant to be shared widely and openly.","message":"- In data-raw/masters.R, also write data/masters.csv (UTF-8, with BOM optional for Excel) and ideally data/masters.parquet (arrow/nanoparquet).\n- Decide how to encode the `||`-separated authors/abstracts in CSV — keep as-is for round-tripping, but document the convention prominently.\n- Consider also publishing data/masters_authors.csv (long format, one row per (id, author)) so analyses that group by author don't need to parse the `||` strings.\n- Make sure non-ASCII characters survive (Norwegian å/ø/æ in titles/authors/abstracts).\n\nDepends on the data dictionary bug — the CSV/Parquet copies should be released together with a dictionary that documents the column semantics, and the dictionary should be authored first so the export step can reference it.\n\nShould also wait until the Oslomet GFU_2024 ingest bug is fixed; otherwise the publicly-released CSV will inherit the 339-row gap.","files":null}]}